<title>BRAZIL: Brazil CVRD selloff is irreversible-paper.</title>
<headline>Brazil CVRD selloff is irreversible-paper.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian Mines and Energy Minister Raimundo Brito said the privatization of mining giant Companhia Vale do Rio Doce is irreversible, despite congressional opposition, newspapers reported.</p>
<p>&quot;I see this opposition as natural,&quot; Brito was quoted by O Globo newspaper as saying, referring to criticism from congressmen and former presidents Jose Sarney and Itamar Franco.</p>
<p>Brito also said Vale will be privatized in February 1997 as scheduled and revenues raised with the company's selloff will be used to reduce public debt, O Globo added.</p>
<p>-- Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo Newsroom, 55-11-248-5412</p>
